1
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:06,130
Damn, I can't see.

2
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:08,380
I scored, Wakabayashi.

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,880
Schneider lands, turns...

4
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:13,550
And shoots!

5
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:16,060
Fire!

6
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:19,890
Wakabayashi!

7
00:00:21,810 --> 00:00:22,650
Damn.

8
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:25,900
Wakabayashi reacts one second too late.

9
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:34,320
Goal!

10
00:00:34,410 --> 00:00:36,080
In the net!

11
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:39,410
In the final match of the first National Youth Tournament in France...

12
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:42,790
In the 22nd minute of the first half...

13
00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:44,790
The German youth score the first goal.

14
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:48,050
We did it! Goal! Schneider did it!

15
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:50,510
Germany scored the first goal!

16
00:00:54,140 --> 00:00:57,100
The fire shot stuck to the net!

17
00:00:57,180 --> 00:01:02,730
Schneider scored magnificent goals in every match of this tournament.

18
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:04,270
Your shot was great!

19
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:06,650
He did it. Well done, Schneider!

20
00:01:07,110 --> 00:01:13,910
Super goalkeeper Wakabayashi couldn't stop it this time.

21
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:14,910
Damn.

22
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:18,620
They finally scored the first goal.

23
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:20,950
We were playing so well...

24
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:25,580
Jito and Margas blocked his view and caused him to be a moment late.

25
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:29,420
So he had predicted this?

26
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:33,550
We won. One goal is enough.

27
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:36,260
We've won this match!

28
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:40,010
Schneider! Schneider!

29
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:42,930
Schneider! Schneider!

30
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:47,810
Schneider raises his right hand to the sky and makes a fist!

31
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:51,190
As if he declared his victory with this goal!

32
00:01:51,980 --> 00:01:55,200
The world youth champion...

33
00:01:55,530 --> 00:01:59,200
will be Karl Heinz Schneider.

34
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:03,830
Did you see, father, mother, Marie?

35
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:10,210
Germany and I have seized victory and become world champions.

36
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,010
Big brother.

37
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:13,920
Karl.

38
00:02:16,470 --> 00:02:18,930
The game starts now!

39
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:20,930
- What?
- Tsubasa!

40
00:02:21,010 --> 00:02:22,470
Are you okay, Tsubasa?

41
00:02:24,350 --> 00:02:28,100
I'm fine. I'm fine. The ball is always my friend.

42
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:30,980
They're only one goal behind!

43
00:02:31,070 --> 00:02:36,150
First we'll equalize, then we'll take the lead, guys!

44
00:02:48,010 --> 00:02:53,290
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

45
00:04:07,110 --> 00:04:10,940
Episode 31
The Strongest Shot in History

46
00:04:16,910 --> 00:04:19,910
This was in Wakabayashi's report.

47
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:22,620
Schneider's coordination with Margas's header...

48
00:04:22,710 --> 00:04:27,340
...striking the loose ball is an old trick for Germany.

49
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:30,510
Yes.

50
00:04:30,590 --> 00:04:33,130
And still, they scored against us.

51
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:34,880
Okay.

52
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:38,390
Then let's make a direct attack too!

53
00:04:38,550 --> 00:04:40,930
Yes, let's do it.

54
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:43,770
Our direct attack is teamwork.

55
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:45,230
Yes.

56
00:04:47,150 --> 00:04:49,020
You're incredible, Tsubasa.

57
00:04:49,110 --> 00:04:53,700
Even after a bitter goal, you brought back the team's fighting spirit.

58
00:04:57,660 --> 00:05:00,660
It's just one goal. They can make up for it!

59
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:03,910
Tsubasa-senpai lifted everyone's spirits.

60
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,040
Yes.

61
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:12,340
Guys, good luck.

62
00:05:19,390 --> 00:05:23,060
Tsubasa. About just now, are you sure you're okay?

63
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:27,650
Yes, I'm fine.

64
00:05:28,270 --> 00:05:30,230
Stubborn dog.

65
00:05:30,690 --> 00:05:32,900
The game restarts.

66
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:38,570
So far, the German youth are ahead.

67
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:41,740
Will this first goal bring them one step closer to the crown?

68
00:05:42,740 --> 00:05:44,750
Anyway, keep trying, Japan.

69
00:05:44,830 --> 00:05:47,670
There is still plenty of time.

70
00:05:49,630 --> 00:05:51,090
Get ready, Misaki.

71
00:05:51,170 --> 00:05:52,000
Okay.

72
00:05:53,090 --> 00:06:00,010
It's started! Japan advances with the golden duo, Tsubasa and Misaki.

73
00:06:01,390 --> 00:06:03,470
So they'll make a direct attack like this.

74
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:05,480
No matter how much of a golden duo you are...

75
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:09,440
...if you insist on a stale trick, you'll lose.

76
00:06:10,150 --> 00:06:16,400
Tsubasa battles one-on-one with Kaltz, and Misaki with Schester.

77
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:17,860
Tsubasa!

78
00:06:17,950 --> 00:06:18,950
Misaki!

79
00:06:20,870 --> 00:06:25,910
Germany has definitely read Japan's attack.

80
00:06:38,510 --> 00:06:40,840
Oh, and Hyuga is there!

81
00:06:40,930 --> 00:06:44,310
He intercepts Tsubasa's pass to Misaki.

82
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:45,470
Good.

83
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,470
What!?

84
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:47,850
Damn it!

85
00:06:48,230 --> 00:06:50,350
Hyuga infiltrates from the center!

86
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:53,270
Japan's strategy succeeded.

87
00:06:55,190 --> 00:06:59,610
Now he transitions from direct dribbling to a shooting position!

88
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:01,110
Catch him!

89
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:07,370
I'll shoot between his legs again!

90
00:07:09,210 --> 00:07:13,250
New Tiger Shot!

91
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:16,300
Catch!

92
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:17,210
Yes.

93
00:07:24,850 --> 00:07:29,270
New Tiger Shot! What power!

94
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:30,640
Great!

95
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:34,310
Nitta goes for the loose ball!

96
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:37,530
In front of the goal and unmarked!

97
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:40,650
Nitta is in a good position.

98
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:43,530
Shoot! Nitta!

99
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:45,410
This goal!

100
00:07:45,950 --> 00:07:49,160
Nitta, between his legs!

101
00:07:49,450 --> 00:07:50,410
Got it!

102
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:52,080
The shot...

103
00:07:52,250 --> 00:07:54,460
Falcon!

104
00:07:59,130 --> 00:08:00,920
Go!

105
00:08:01,340 --> 00:08:02,430
Müller!

106
00:08:05,890 --> 00:08:06,930
It went through!

107
00:08:09,970 --> 00:08:11,810
No, it didn't!

108
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:13,390
What!?

109
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:20,280
Goalkeeper Müller very comfortably caught it from behind with his hand.

110
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:24,700
He deliberately let it go through.

111
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:28,530
This is what you wanted, isn't it, coach?

112
00:08:30,370 --> 00:08:34,460
Exactly. Now you have no more weak points.

113
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:41,880
Useless. That goalkeeper has no weak points.

114
00:08:46,050 --> 00:08:50,970
Was my forward instinct just an illusion?

115
00:08:51,470 --> 00:08:53,230
I won't give up!

116
00:08:53,770 --> 00:08:54,850
Tsubasa!

117
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:58,190
He might appear to have no weak points!

118
00:08:58,270 --> 00:09:02,610
But there is no completely invincible goalkeeper in the world!

119
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:07,370
Tsubasa swiftly prevents the ball from reaching Mayer.

120
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:08,740
What!?

121
00:09:08,870 --> 00:09:10,330
Great, Tsubasa.

122
00:09:10,410 --> 00:09:12,370
Good, go!

123
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:16,420
Ozora Tsubasa, you're a kid who shows his strength in difficulty.

124
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,880
Well done, Tsubasa.

125
00:09:19,250 --> 00:09:24,760
The more you pressure him, the stronger he comes back.

126
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:26,840
That's Ozora Tsubasa.

127
00:09:26,970 --> 00:09:30,350
Our pillar, Captain Tsubasa.

128
00:09:30,930 --> 00:09:33,350
Damn. Come on, let's reinforce the defense.

129
00:09:37,850 --> 00:09:39,770
Just look at his speed!

130
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:43,400
Tsubasa bursts through the German defense one by one.

131
00:09:45,030 --> 00:09:46,990
Together, Hyuga.

132
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,360
Tsubasa!

133
00:09:48,610 --> 00:09:52,240
So you were thinking the same as me?

134
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:55,790
When we both went for the ball at the free kick...

135
00:09:56,290 --> 00:09:59,580
...you were thinking of combining the shots to surprise them.

136
00:09:59,670 --> 00:10:01,040
Isn't that right?

137
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:08,590
Those two...

138
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:15,430
I can't believe it!

139
00:10:15,770 --> 00:10:17,520
I can't believe it.

140
00:10:17,770 --> 00:10:22,020
Tsubasa and Hyuga decided to strike at the same time.

141
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:25,940
The two rivals are now cooperating.

142
00:10:26,190 --> 00:10:30,410
So are they finally acting together?

143
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,280
Can they do this?

144
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:33,660
Tsubasa!

145
00:10:33,870 --> 00:10:34,790
Kojiro!

146
00:10:34,950 --> 00:10:36,000
Tsubasa!

147
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:37,000
Hyuga!

148
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:38,540
Good luck!

149
00:10:38,710 --> 00:10:39,830
Tsubasa!

150
00:10:39,920 --> 00:10:40,790
Senpai!

151
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:42,380
Tsubasa!

152
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:43,420
Hyuga-san!

153
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:44,920
Shoot!

154
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:50,430
Drive Shot!

155
00:10:50,510 --> 00:10:52,640
Tiger Shot!

156
00:10:53,010 --> 00:10:57,350
Incredible! Tsubasa and Hyuga strike at the same time!

157
00:10:57,430 --> 00:11:00,060
The Drive Shot and Tiger Shot combine!

158
00:11:00,140 --> 00:11:03,020
This is a twin Drive Tiger Shot!

159
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:09,900
It could also be called a Tiger Drive in reverse...

160
00:11:09,990 --> 00:11:12,660
...but they struck in perfect harmony!

161
00:11:12,870 --> 00:11:14,330
Go!

162
00:11:14,410 --> 00:11:16,160
We've equalized!

163
00:11:16,450 --> 00:11:18,620
This is Japan's secret weapon!

164
00:11:18,710 --> 00:11:22,420
The strongest shot of the century is fired!

165
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:28,970
The power and spin of the Tiger and Drive shots made the ball tremble.

166
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:31,550
More than our twin shot...

167
00:11:31,630 --> 00:11:34,140
More than Tsubasa and Misaki's twin shot...

168
00:11:34,220 --> 00:11:36,180
Its vibration is extraordinarily abnormal!

169
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:37,850
As is its speed!

170
00:11:37,970 --> 00:11:41,350
This is a goal now. It will definitely be a goal!

171
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:42,730
Müller!

172
00:11:42,980 --> 00:11:44,610
You can catch it, Müller.

173
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:48,230
Coach.

174
00:11:53,410 --> 00:11:55,410
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

175
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,930
Born: August 10 | Height: 193 cm
Weight: 96 kg | Blood Type: O

176
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:25,080
Now your final training.

177
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:26,370
Yes, coach.

178
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:37,340
It's not easy. I will throw three soccer balls.

179
00:12:37,430 --> 00:12:39,140
You must catch them.

180
00:12:41,350 --> 00:12:44,890
But I will also throw other things.

181
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:46,140
What!?

182
00:13:06,790 --> 00:13:07,620
Coach!

183
00:13:07,710 --> 00:13:09,960
Don't give in to fear, Müller!

184
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:15,300
With calm assessment and wild reflexes, you can catch them!

185
00:13:15,630 --> 00:13:17,180
O- Okay, coach.

186
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:27,440
The first!

187
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:38,650
Coming!

188
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:52,000
The second!

189
00:14:02,390 --> 00:14:03,220
And this is the third.

190
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:19,700
There!

191
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:35,170
H- He caught it! Müller stops this shot!

192
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,380
Wh- What!?

193
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:38,420
Impossible!

194
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:46,510
The third!

195
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:55,520
That's it. You're amazing, Müller.

196
00:14:55,610 --> 00:14:59,820
No one, absolutely no one can score against you.

197
00:15:00,110 --> 00:15:03,530
Germany's goalkeeper, Dieter Müller...

198
00:15:03,610 --> 00:15:09,080
...catches Tsubasa and Hyuga's twin Drive Tiger Shot!

199
00:15:09,870 --> 00:15:11,790
Well done, Müller.

200
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:13,330
Great catch.

201
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:18,340
Impossible! Tsubasa and Hyuga's twin shot too?

202
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:23,840
But how did he catch it?

203
00:15:31,390 --> 00:15:32,640
No.

204
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:38,110
Hyuga, that injury you got in the France match...

205
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:41,860
I'm fine, Tsubasa.

206
00:15:43,490 --> 00:15:46,240
I still haven't given up.

207
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:53,250
Worthy of my reputation as Japan's best forward, I will score against him at all costs.

208
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:54,960
Yes.

209
00:15:56,830 --> 00:16:02,800
Right. There's no giving up in the Japanese youth's dictionary.

210
00:16:07,180 --> 00:16:08,010
Catch!

211
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:10,520
Müller gets up!

212
00:16:15,060 --> 00:16:17,190
It reached Schneider!

213
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:19,520
Go after him.

214
00:16:20,190 --> 00:16:23,320
Schneider, who was standing a bit behind on the field...

215
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:26,320
...advances by dribbling.

216
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:28,620
The Japanese defense...

217
00:16:28,700 --> 00:16:35,290
...might be shaken by the stopping of Tsubasa and Hyuga's twin shot.

218
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:37,500
You can't go any further.

219
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:39,790
You can't score the second goal.

220
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:42,010
Guys, defend with all your strength.

221
00:16:42,090 --> 00:16:43,260
Okay!

222
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:47,680
The Japanese defense seems unbreakable.

223
00:16:50,140 --> 00:16:55,480
They go to take the ball from Schneider with tight defense.

224
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:05,700
Even if he passes, they quickly catch up and surround him.

225
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:08,450
What fighting spirit!

226
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:09,870
Guys!

227
00:17:10,490 --> 00:17:11,910
I won't let him pass.

228
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:16,580
We must take the ball and pass it to Tsubasa and the others.

229
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:20,040
Tsubasa... We...

230
00:17:20,130 --> 00:17:23,210
We're not giving up on victory.

231
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:27,930
Even Schneider can't pass and shoot.

232
00:17:28,470 --> 00:17:30,470
So this is the Japanese fighting spirit?

233
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,600
Schneider, this way.

234
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:39,230
Schneider gave up on penetrating the defense...

235
00:17:39,310 --> 00:17:40,860
...and passed to the corner.

236
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:42,860
No.

237
00:17:43,190 --> 00:17:47,950
It's Schester. A beautiful pass goes to the free Schester.

238
00:17:48,030 --> 00:17:48,860
Great!

239
00:17:49,530 --> 00:17:50,620
This goal!

240
00:17:51,030 --> 00:17:52,490
Please, Wakabayashi.

241
00:17:52,990 --> 00:17:53,990
Wakabayashi!

242
00:17:54,290 --> 00:17:55,240
Okay.

243
00:17:55,830 --> 00:17:59,000
Wakabayashi reacts quickly to the shot.

244
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:00,880
Go!

245
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:06,880
Oh, Wakabayashi doesn't catch it, he kicks it directly.

246
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:08,130
What!?

247
00:18:08,220 --> 00:18:09,470
Wakabayashi!

248
00:18:09,550 --> 00:18:10,640
Well done!

249
00:18:10,890 --> 00:18:14,970
Now the ball heads back toward the German goal!

250
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:18,140
Suddenly the tables turned.

251
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,520
Hyuga, I trust you.

252
00:18:20,900 --> 00:18:21,770
Okay.

253
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:23,060
Hyuga-san!

254
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,520
Takeshi!

255
00:18:25,190 --> 00:18:27,740
Tsubasa runs toward the goal!

256
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:30,660
Sawada takes his place.

257
00:18:31,570 --> 00:18:33,280
You know what to do, Takeshi.

258
00:18:33,450 --> 00:18:34,370
Yes.

259
00:18:35,950 --> 00:18:39,500
Oh, the ball came behind them.

260
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:43,670
And now this time, Hyuga and Sawada strike simultaneously.

261
00:18:44,250 --> 00:18:45,550
Go!

262
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:52,050
This is the Toho Golden Duo's overhead kick and scissor combination.

263
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:55,140
I'll show you that this kind of shot doesn't work on me.

264
00:18:55,220 --> 00:18:57,430
Didn't you see what just happened?

265
00:18:57,810 --> 00:18:59,930
The ball is vibrating!

266
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:04,360
Besides, the ball in the previous shot was moving more.

267
00:19:04,610 --> 00:19:06,440
This is child's play.

268
00:19:09,570 --> 00:19:10,950
It deflected!

269
00:19:11,450 --> 00:19:12,450
What!?

270
00:19:12,660 --> 00:19:14,620
That wasn't a shot!

271
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:19,330
The vibrating ball suddenly changed direction to the right! This is a pass!

272
00:19:19,580 --> 00:19:22,920
There is a big difference between Hyuga-san's and my shooting power.

273
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,590
It's natural for the ball to veer to the right.

274
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:29,920
Please, Misaki.

275
00:19:30,130 --> 00:19:31,050
Okay!

276
00:19:31,130 --> 00:19:32,930
Misaki jumps!

277
00:19:33,010 --> 00:19:37,350
This pass was intended for Misaki running toward the goal.

278
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:38,470
Müller!

279
00:19:40,850 --> 00:19:44,850
Misaki executes his favorite technique, the diving header!

280
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:48,190
But Müller catches it!

281
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:50,440
Despite the consecutive attacks...

282
00:19:50,530 --> 00:19:54,160
Japan cannot infiltrate the steel giant Müller's goal.

283
00:19:54,530 --> 00:19:56,620
Misaki, hold on.

284
00:19:57,990 --> 00:19:59,240
I'm coming!

285
00:20:01,580 --> 00:20:03,750
Go, Misaki!

286
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:08,130
Tsubasa, from behind Misaki whose diving header was blocked...

287
00:20:08,210 --> 00:20:10,630
...catches up and gives extra power with both feet!

288
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:14,630
What!?

289
00:20:28,730 --> 00:20:31,480
In the net! Goal!

290
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:35,070
They finally broke through Müller's goal.

291
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:38,830
The ball and Misaki are thrown into the German goal.

292
00:20:38,910 --> 00:20:40,790
Equalizer!

293
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:46,670
In the 25th minute of the first half, Japan ties it 1-1.

294
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,580
Hoooooray!

295
00:20:48,670 --> 00:20:52,460
You're extraordinary, Tsubasa and Misaki.

296
00:20:58,680 --> 00:21:00,720
You did it, Tsubasa!

297
00:21:00,810 --> 00:21:02,310
Misaki!

298
00:21:02,390 --> 00:21:04,680
Yes! We did it!

299
00:21:06,850 --> 00:21:09,230
We've equalized!

300
00:21:10,310 --> 00:21:13,440
We finally scored against Müller.

301
00:21:15,740 --> 00:21:19,160
Tsubasa... You really...

302
00:21:20,620 --> 00:21:21,870
Misaki.

303
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:22,990
Tsubasa.

304
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:25,910
Unbe... unbelievable Nankatsu...

305
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:30,460
I mean, Japan's golden duo, Tsubasa and Misaki.

306
00:21:32,170 --> 00:21:33,460
We did it!

307
00:21:33,590 --> 00:21:36,840
You're unique, Tsubasa! Great support!

308
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:39,840
Hyuga and Takeshi, your passes were also great.

309
00:21:40,140 --> 00:21:42,600
Misaki, your header was perfect.

310
00:21:42,680 --> 00:21:46,730
This goal, thanks to the Toho Golden Duo's fascinating pass...

311
00:21:46,810 --> 00:21:50,860
...the defense's determination to stop Schneider...

312
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:53,940
...and Wakabayashi's strike...

313
00:21:54,030 --> 00:21:56,610
...turning danger into a golden opportunity.

314
00:21:56,860 --> 00:22:00,240
This is a team victory for Japan!

315
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:04,240
The team scored the equalizer by bonding and working together!

316
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:50,040
NEXT EPISODE
A SHATTERED HAT